# Source Excel workbook: kept locally as the source of truth for
# extract_data.py, but never needed by the deployed site (index.html has
# the data embedded directly) and may contain personal info (see the HR
# sheet exclusion in RULES.md) that shouldn't end up in a public repo's
# history. If you want it version-controlled somewhere, do that
# separately/privately -- don't remove this line without thinking about
# where the file is about to be published.
*.xlsx

# Ephemeral sync artifacts (see RULES.md section 12 / extract_data.py) --
# extracted_questions.json is a debugging intermediate that only survives
# a failed run; *.bak files are the safety backups clear_data.py/
# add_sheets.py/smart_sync.py/extract_data.py write before overwriting
# index.html. Neither is meant to be committed.
extracted_questions.json
*.bak

# Python bytecode cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
